    "created_at": "2020-09-03T17:05:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-09-03T17:05:04Z",
    "body": "Quoted from the [form-element spec](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#the-form-element):\r\n\r\n> The elements IDL attribute must return an HTMLFormControlsCollection rooted at the form element's root, whose filter matches listed elements whose form owner is the form element, with the exception of input elements whose type attribute is in the Image Button state, which must, for historical reasons, be excluded from this particular collection.\r\n\r\n> Listed elements\r\n> Denotes elements that are listed in the form.elements and fieldset.elements APIs. These elements also have a form content attribute, and a matching form IDL attribute, that allow authors to specify an explicit form owner.\r\n> button, fieldset, input, object, output, select, textarea, form-associated custom elements\r\n\r\nIn my humble opinion there seems to be a difference between the spec and the behaviour or am I wrong?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/686628531/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
